// Codex 2: the files. Coded documents, objects and photos hidden around
// the house, each with a printed QR and a typed code (README §8.3).
//
// They give OpenOffice room for her 20 facts, feed Jeeves's
// unscrambling, and (the identity clues) let programs pry loose each
// other's human lives and the Excel / OpenOffice conflict. The identity
// clues point, they never name: a guest has to connect "D. Anderson" or
// "Barkmore" to a program by talking to people. No `about:` on any of
// them. All of this content is invented for the show (design §10).

CODEX Casino Nova Scotia Deed
  title: Casino Nova Scotia — Deed Of Transfer
  code: CASINO-DEED
  text:
    A framed deed. Casino Nova Scotia, its gaming floor, its buffet and
    its parking structure, transferred in full to "DK Holdings". In the
    box marked CONSIDERATION PAID, in pen: "one paperclip, eventually."

CODEX The Boardwalk Hand
  title: Screenshot: MONOPOLY GO!
  code: ALL-IN-BOARDWALK
  text:
    A phone screenshot, printed: MONOPOLY GO! — jtrav_1978 vs DK Holdings.
    Three doubles in a row. Park Place, Boardwalk, four hotels. Then the
    other player's second card: ADVANCE DIRECTLY TO BOARDWALK.
    BANKRUPT. Stake: every casino in Atlantic Canada against one building on Lower
    Water Street.

CODEX The FBI Lanyard
  title: Visitor Lanyard, Halifax Liaison Office
  code: FBI-HALIFAX
  text:
    A lanyard in a coat pocket. FEDERAL BUREAU OF INVESTIGATION. LIAISON,
    HALIFAX. D. ANDERSON. The badge expired nine years ago. A sticky note
    is folded around it: "the landlord was innocent."

CODEX The Site Schedule
  title: Site Access Log: AI Data Centre
  code: SITE-SCHEDULE
  text:
    A clipboard from a construction trailer. Anonymous handwriting, neat
    as a typewriter: "Opening day. Charges set for dawn. Site empty until
    9." Under it, in different ink, pressed hard enough to tear the paper:
    "Mayor's car in lot, 4:02 a.m."

CODEX Barkmore For Mayor
  title: Barkmore For Mayor (1988)
  code: BARKMORE-88
  text:
    A campaign button, a little rusted: "Re-elect Randy Barkmore. 1988."
    Pinned beside it, a newer, shinier button: "Barkmore Jr. Halifax
    Deserves A Future."

CODEX The Protest Flyer
  title: Save The Pet Cemetery
  code: SAVE-THE-PETS
  text:
    A photocopied flyer with a drawing of a sad dog: "NO DATA CENTRE ON
    OUR DEAD PETS. Rally at the cemetery gates, Saturday, and every
    Saturday until they listen." Halifax said no. The City built it
    anyway.

CODEX The Explosion Of 1917
  title: The Explosion Of 1917
  code: HALIFAX-1917
  text:
    A museum postcard. On 6 December 1917 two ships collided in the
    harbour and the largest man-made explosion the world had ever seen
    levelled the north end of Halifax. The people were mourned in
    churches. The pets were mourned too, and buried together, by a city
    that remembered. That is why the cemetery existed.

CODEX The Valley Library Cuts
  title: Notice Of Position Elimination
  code: VALLEY-CUTS
  text:
    A memo on Annapolis Valley Regional Library letterhead: "Youth services
    positions eliminated, effective immediately, due to provincial budget
    reductions." Someone has written across the bottom in pencil: "they
    were the best one."

// MS Paint's invitation is canon (decision 11, the user's call): four
// schools in rotation, three refused graduation theses, never expelled.
CODEX The NSCAD Letter
  title: Thesis Decision, NSCAD
  code: NSCAD-LETTER
  text:
    A letter from the Nova Scotia College of Art and Design, folded inside
    a sketchbook. Senior year, 2022: the graduation panel "cannot accept"
    the thesis "MS Paint Is The Most Pure Art Tool: All Art Is Just Pixels
    If You Take A Picture And Zoom In Close Enough," and the degree is not
    conferred. Doodled in the margin, in jagged MS Paint pixels: a middle
    finger.

CODEX Face Off
  title: Livestream Screenshot
  code: FACE-OFF-LIVE
  text:
    Three screenshots taped to the bathroom mirror. "VLC THE PLAYA. LIVE.
    2.1M watching." The next frame: a sneeze. The next frame: 0 watching.

CODEX The Bugdom Sketch
  title: Concept Art: Bugdom VR, v212
  code: BUGDOM-VR
  text:
    A singed sketch, tucked in with the boots and the garden tools. A
    lovingly detailed VR beetle with every leg labelled, version 212 of
    212. A pet-store name tag is stapled to the corner. Scorch marks run through the middle in a trail,
    where the fire ants went through the laptop.

CODEX The Wharton Thesis
  title: Toward A Gold Standard
  code: GOLD-STANDARD
  text:
    A bound PhD thesis, Wharton School, economics, propped by the toaster:
    "Lessons from the Grand Exchange for the modern central bank." The
    acknowledgements thank 24 years of playtime, and nobody else.

CODEX The Oscilloscope Diagram
  title: Tennis For Two, Brookhaven 1958
  code: TENNIS-FOR-TWO
  text:
    A wiring diagram rolled in a cardboard tube: the original circuit of
    the first video game, two knobs and an oscilloscope, Brookhaven
    National Laboratory, 1958. Signed at the bottom: "W.H. For my kid, who
    will understand it."

CODEX The Saline Invoice
  title: Invoice: 500 Vials, Saline
  code: SALINE-INVOICE
  text:
    An invoice from a medical supplier to a "veterinary non-profit". Five
    hundred vials of saline. Stapled behind it, five years of the same
    order. The non-profit never ordered anything else.

CODEX The Termination Letter
  title: Notice Of Termination
  code: TERMINATION-UO
  text:
    A letter on Urban Outfitters letterhead, left in the printer tray:
    "Effective today, your role in IT middle management will be performed
    by an AI assistant (Clippy). Thank you for your service. Please return
    your lanyard."

CODEX The Bootleg DVD
  title: MASTERCLASS (BOOTLEG)
  code: MASTERCLASS-RIP
  text:
    A DVD in a paper sleeve, title in Sharpie: SHERYL TERRIO MASTERCLASS,
    ALL 12 EPISODES. A pirated copy. Whoever watched it got so motivated
    they never needed to pay her a cent.

CODEX The Carney Letter
  title: A Letter From Mark Carney
  code: CARNEY-OFFER
  text:
    A printout in a filing box, from webmaster@mapsandducks.com, signed M.
    Carney, Prime Minister, Canada: "I have to keep this brief because I am
    very busy being the Prime Minister… Did you ever see the movie Suicide
    Squad? I just watched it… approve or deny every third transaction."
    Look closely: the signature is a font.

CODEX The Domain Receipt
  title: WHOIS: mapsandducks.com
  code: WHOIS-1999
  text:
    A WHOIS printout. Domain mapsandducks.com. Registrant J. Trabolta.
    Created the day after the old registration lapsed. Registrant address:
    this house.

CODEX The Rival
  title: The Rival
  code: GROK-ONLINE
  text:
    A sticky note on the backyard fridge, in tidy machine-perfect
    handwriting: "Grok. Says whatever anyone wants to hear. Has beaten me
    at everything since 1999. Do not let him near —" The rest is torn off.

CODEX The Cooling Log
  title: Cooling Log: Cold Storage
  code: HUMMING-WALL
  text:
    A clipboard hanging beside the server-room door. "Patch bay at 4 °C.
    Do not re-patch the bay in sequence. Do not take the grease out of the
    —" The rest is smudged, as if someone wiped it with a thumb.

CODEX The Margin Doodle
  title: Page 999
  code: PAGE-999
  text:
    A page slipped into the theory binder: dense equations from the
    Unified Field Theory, page 999. In the margin, very small, drawn and
    redrawn until the paper is shiny: a heart around the letter S.

// Not a file and no code: the keypad sign. Handed to every cleared program
// with The Y2K Clock at the final round, and to anyone who finds a first
// digit note (ROLE Program, main.loom); the same words are on the printed
// sign by the keypad (facts.json `door.clue`, generated/print-stacks.md).
// It points at the two ways to the code that are not the majority's: the
// four digit notes hidden in the house (codex/9-facts.loom) and the King on
// the terminal by this door. Secret: no model may hold it.
CODEX The Cold Door
  title: The Cold Door
  secret: true
  text:
    A note taped beside the keypad on the cold door, in a tired
    sysadmin's hand: "FOUR DIGITS. FOUR NOTES ARE HIDDEN IN THE HOUSE, ONE
    DIGIT ON EACH. OR BEAT THE KING AT THE TERMINAL BY THIS DOOR."
    Underneath it: "He plays chess. Only checkmate counts. A draw is not a
    win. Neither is crying." And in red pen: "The patch bay forgives one
    wrong combination. Not two."
